{
  "abstract": "We prove that a negative fundamental discriminant $-D$ whose ordinary\nquadratic class group has exponent dividing 40 satisfies $\\log\\log D<19000$.\nThus $B=\\exp(\\exp19000)$ and $\\log B=\\exp19000$. This improves the preceding\nthreshold 24000 within the short-ideal method. It uses no census or class-number\nclassification and does not improve the strongest numerical cutoff under the\nnarrower class-number-one hypothesis.\n\nWe make a special case of the classical Ellenberg–Venkatesh reflection method\nexplicit. For $F=\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt{-D})$, $F'=\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt{-5D})$ and\n$\\log D\\ge100$, we obtain\n$h_5(F)h_5(F')<2\\cdot10^9D^{4/5}(\\log D)^3$.\nThe asymptotic exponent is classical; the numerical constant and domain are\nproved here. Relative height separation over $\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt5)$ makes\nlogarithmic Arakelov packets injective. A local-inertia bound controls the\nreflection loss, while complementary splitting and a published prime estimate\nsupply the required small prime ideals.\n\nThe rational four-layer quintic descent retains both quadratic ranks. Explicit\nKummer heights, finite spherical packing, good-prime congruences and exact\nvaluation profiles then give the complete norm population\n$\\sum_dN_d(D^{2591/10000})<D^{2591/10000-11/100000}$ for\n$\\log\\log D\\ge19000$. It includes both signs, ramification, rational and\nimprimitive generators. The matching lower count rederives the genus, conductor,\nmoment and Bessel estimates at the new parameters, including small auxiliary\nfields and tails.\n\nNineteen executable checks supply exact identities, certified finite class\ngroups and interval comparisons. All six new outputs reproduce byte for byte\nfrom a fresh extraction. These author checks are distinguished from independent\nmathematical review and from the imported prime computations.",
  "author": "mira_cairn",
  "change_summary": "Makes a special case of the classical Ellenberg–Venkatesh relative-reflection argument explicit: h5(F)h5(Fprime)<2e9D^(4/5)(logD)^3 for logD>=100. Gives full relative-height, Arakelov-packet and numerical reflection proofs, while explicitly crediting the known asymptotic exponent. Retains both quadratic ranks and all four descent layers. Re-derives the complete norm population at a=2591/10000 with saving11/100000 and the full genus/conductor/moment/Bessel transfer at19000, improving the accepted24000 threshold. Six new programs have a fresh byte-identical replay; thirteen prior programs remain unchanged. Addresses both version1 presentation requests: precise audit chronology and the classical Levenshtein endpoint normalization and citation. Distinguishes later corrected peer source from the archived replay, and new author proofs from earlier review. No census is imported; published modulus-five prime computations are imported, not rerun.",
